From fce5de6518c602fcc2e577477f8e38d39e094dde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joonhoekim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:31:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/61] soc: qcom: pmic_glink_altmode: handle notifications on
 the freezable workqueue

Unplugging a DisplayPort alt-mode sink while the system is in s2idle
makes the firmware send an alt-mode notification. The glink interrupt
wakes a CPU, the altmode work runs right away on system_wq, and it
reprograms the orientation switch and the Type-C mux while every device
is still suspended:

  i2c i2c-2: Transfer while suspended
  WARNING: drivers/i2c/i2c-core.h:57 at __i2c_transfer
  Workqueue: events pmic_glink_altmode_worker
   fsa4480_set / fsa4480_switch_set / typec_switch_set

after which (Lenovo TB323FU, kaanapali) the s2idle loop never resumes,
the power key does nothing and the board ends up in download mode.

Queue the work on system_freezable_wq instead: a notification that
arrives during suspend is then handled after the tasks are thawed, with
the I2C controller and the PHY resumed.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
index 13c434f8d..465e5d231 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/pmic_glink_altmode.c
@@ -451,7 +451,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8180xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 	alt_port->mode = mode;
 	alt_port->hpd_state = hpd_state;
 	alt_port->hpd_irq = hpd_irq;
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 #define SC8280XP_DPAM_MASK	0x3f
@@ -502,7 +502,7 @@ static void pmic_glink_altmode_sc8280xp_notify(struct pmic_glink_altmode *altmod
 		alt_port->tbt_data = *tbt;
 	}
 
-	schedule_work(&alt_port->work);
+	queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &alt_port->work);
 }
 
 static void pmic_glink_altmode_callback(const void *data, size_t len, void *priv)
-- 
